implementationPlan.description:
TESTS FIRST (RED). In scripts/tests/postflight-worktree.cjs (shared by postflight.sh and postflight.ps1), add `async function wtFollowLock()` directly after wtFollowRace. Register it with its own statement right after the `Object.assign(cases,{...});` line: `cases['wt-follow-lock']=wtFollowLock;`. Peers edit that one long line, so do not touch it. Edit with the Edit tool. Leave every existing case, the follows[] table and the PATH git stub unchanged; the 'lock' row stays byte-identical (DoD 3). These scenarios set no WT_GIT_* knob, so the real git runs (on ps1, git.ps1 runs in-process and would hide native stderr from the lock check).

Counting: launch() passes knobs into the wrapper env, so set GIT_TRACE to an absolute file under root, one per scenario. Git appends `trace: built-in: git merge -q --ff-only --no-autostash <sha>` for every merge it runs, and only the follow passes --no-autostash (sh ~:6736, ps1 ~:6123). Helpers:
- merges=f=>(readOr(f)||'').split('\n').filter(l=>/trace: built-in: git merge .*--no-autostash/.test(l)).length;
- behinds=r=>(r.log.match(/^\[WARN\] MOE_CONTROL_CHECKOUT_BEHIND: /gm)||[]).length (one [WARN] line per follow that gave up, whatever the #general throttle does);
- lockOf=p=>path.join(git(p.top,'rev-parse','--absolute-git-dir').trim(),'index.lock').
Probed with git 2.43: a merge blocked by a held lock exits 1 with "error: Unable to create '<gitdir>/index.lock': File exists.", and GIT_TRACE prints that built-in line once per merge.

Scenario 'released' (DoD 2): p=repo('wt-follow-lock-released'); old=mainOf(p); tip=commitOn(p,'refs/heads/main',{'src/b.txt':'b\n'}); write the lock as ''. Run launch(p,'wt-follow-lock-released',{GIT_TRACE:t},{signal}). signal is polled every 100 ms and always returns false, so nothing is signalled. It records started=Date.now() once merges(t)>=1; 3 s after that it records gone=!present(lock), removes the lock and sets removed=true. Assert, each message ending in tail(r.log):
- the MOE_CONTROL_ codes in the log are exactly ['MOE_CONTROL_ADVANCED'], with one `[OK] MOE_CONTROL_ADVANCED old..tip` line;
- removed is true and gone is false ('the wrapper deleted index.lock');
- merges(t)>=2 (at least one retry);
- the symbolic HEAD is refs/heads/moe/control at tip, and main is tip;
- r.code===0 && r.cliRan.
If the scenario fails before the removal, remove the lock in a finally.

Scenario 'held' (DoD 1 cap): a lock held for the whole launch, with GIT_TRACE. Assert:
- behinds(r)>=1 and merges(t)===5*behinds(r) (5 tries per follow);
- the lock is still present (then remove it);
- no ADVANCED line, and HEAD is still old;
- r.code===0 && r.cliRan.

Scenario 'other' (DoD 4): no lock. Write src/a.txt as 'human edit\n' in the control checkout, then tip=commitOn(p,'refs/heads/main',{'src/a.txt':'landed\n'}) (the follows 'edit' setup). Assert:
- behinds(r)>=1 and merges(t)===behinds(r) (a non-lock merge failure is never retried);
- the edit is kept, and HEAD is still old;
- r.code===0 && r.cliRan.

Error handling in the test: every assertion names its scenario and ends with tail(r.log); the trace and lock paths sit under the suite's root, so its own cleanup removes them.

RED proof before step 2, sh only, from the worktree root:
T=$(mktemp -d) && cp scripts/tests/postflight-fake-proxy.js "$T/fake-proxy.js" && MOE_WORKTREE_ONLY=wt-follow-lock,wt-follow env -u MOE_SESSION_ID -u MOE_ATTEMPT_ID -u MOE_ATTEMPT_GENERATION node scripts/tests/postflight-worktree.cjs sh "$PWD/scripts/moe-agent.sh" "$T/fake-proxy.js" "$T" "$(command -v bash)"
Expect 'wt-follow-lock FAILED' on 'released' (codes [MOE_CONTROL_CHECKOUT_BEHIND], no ADVANCED) and 'wt-follow ok'. Keep that tail. mem:gotcha-postflight-worktree-mutant-copy has this loop and its Windows variant.

FIX the twin, Invoke-MoeControlFollow in scripts/moe-agent.ps1, with the Edit tool (keep the UTF-8 BOM and LF). Replace the block from `# The checked tip, not the ref:` through the MOE_CONTROL_ADVANCED Write-Host with:
        # The checked tip, not the ref: a target that moved since carries unchecked .moe paths.
        # A held .git/index.lock (the IDE's git, a peer's landing or follow) is retried like
        # Update-MoeSharedIndex: at most 5 tries, 2 s apart. Any other failure is final. Never delete the lock.
        for ($attempt = 1; $attempt -le 5; $attempt++) {
            $m = Invoke-MoeGit -Top $top -GitArgs @('-c', "core.hooksPath=$hooks", 'merge', '-q', '--ff-only', '--no-autostash', $tip) -MergeStderr
            $new = & $one (Invoke-MoeGit -Top $top -GitArgs @('rev-parse', '-q', '--verify', 'HEAD^{commit}'))
            if ($m.Rc -eq 0) { break }
            # A peer's follow that held the index lock may already have moved HEAD to the tip.
            if ($new -and (Invoke-MoeGit -Top $top -GitArgs @('merge-base', '--is-ancestor', $tip, $new)).Rc -eq 0) { return }
            $err = $m.Out -join "`n"
            if ($attempt -lt 5 -and $err -like '*index.lock*') { Start-Sleep -Seconds 2; continue }
            if ($err.Length -gt 1500) { $err = $err.Substring(0, 1500) }
            Send-MoeControlAlert 'MOE_CONTROL_CHECKOUT_BEHIND' "moe/control stays at $old, behind $target at ${tip}: $err" $git; return
        }
        if ($new -cne $old) { Write-Host "[OK] MOE_CONTROL_ADVANCED $old..$new" -ForegroundColor Green }
Every return stays inside the existing try/finally, so the temp hooks dir is still removed on every path. Error handling is as in step 2: no new code, message or log line, so the codes case and parity-check's code-family diff stay unchanged. Parse check: [System.Management.Automation.Language.Parser]::ParseFile reports no errors under both powershell.exe and pwsh.exe (mem:gotcha-launcher-ps1-rows-from-wsl).

ADVERSARIAL SELF-REVIEW of your own diff, then handoff.
(1) Mutants. Put each in its own copy of the snapshot's whole scripts/ (mem:gotcha-postflight-worktree-mutant-copy), and run an unmutated control copy first. Use the sh subset MOE_WORKTREE_ONLY=wt-follow-lock.
- M1: drop the `[[ "$err" == *index.lock* ]]` test, so every failure retries. It must fail 'other'.
- M2: cap at 3 tries. It must fail 'held'.
- M3: remove `sleep 2`. It must fail 'released'.
- On ps1, run M1 on a BOM-preserving copy. It must fail 'other'.
A mutant that drops the in-loop HEAD re-check is expected to survive. A merge with HEAD already at the tip exits 0 without taking the lock (probed, git 2.43), so the shortcut is reachable only between a failed merge and the next HEAD read; confirm it by reading both twins.
(2) Re-read both twins and confirm:
- every try merges the checked $tip;
- sh resets rc on each try;
- there is no sleep after the last try;
- the ps1 returns stay inside the try/finally;
- no path deletes a lock;
- the non-lock BEHIND text and the hourly alert throttle are unchanged.
`git diff` must touch only the two follow blocks, the sh local line, the new case and its registration line.
(3) Edges:
- an IDE lock held for more than 8 s ends BEHIND exactly as today, and the QA landed gate then stops the seat as today;
- with two followers at once, each takes the lock in turn, and the loser's retry or its HEAD re-check covers it;
- the worst-case added delay is 8 s per follow, at the loop top and at pre-flight.
(4) Serena write_memory 'task-task-a837dd48fcb049b5a54681aae1edfc79-handoff', with the timings and the mutant results. Then complete_task with step 4's evidence.
